# Audio and MetaSound Tools (UE 5.6)

This focused toolset uses only APIs present in Unreal Engine 5.6.1. It covers the highest-value first pass without introducing a second graph framework or any UnrealMCP runtime dependency.

The base `UnrealMCP` plugin does not enable MetaSound for the host project.
SoundWave and SoundCue routes remain part of the base plugin. To author a
MetaSound, explicitly enable both the UE 5.6 `Metasound` plugin and the
editor-only `UnrealMCPMetaSound` companion plugin in the target project, then
restart the editor.

If either opt-in plugin is disabled, `create_basic_metasound_source` remains in
the public MCP catalog but returns `dependency_plugin_disabled` with
`required_plugins` and `disabled_plugins`. This is a pre-dispatch failure with
`mutation_attempted=false`, `mutation_performed=false`, and `changed=false`;
enable the listed plugins and restart instead of retrying the mutation.

## Tools

- `list_audio_assets(directory="/Game", recursive=true, max_results=200, offset=0)`
  - Lists `SoundWave`, `SoundCue`, and `MetaSoundSource` assets with deterministic bounded pagination.
- `inspect_audio_asset(asset_path)`
  - Reads common asset metadata. SoundWaves include duration and channel count; SoundCues include root/node information; MetaSounds are identified as standard engine assets. It does not claim that arbitrary existing assets are free of UnrealMCP references without auditing their authored graph.
- `create_sound_cue_from_wave(name, sound_wave_path, package_path="/Game/Audio/SoundCues")`
  - Creates and saves a SoundCue with exactly one standard `SoundNodeWavePlayer` root. Saved readback must reference the requested SoundWave exactly.
- `create_basic_metasound_source(name, package_path="/Game/Audio/MetaSounds", oscillator="sine", frequency=440.0, output_format="mono")`
  - Creates a continuous source through UE 5.6 `UMetaSoundEditorSubsystem::BuildToAsset`. Supported generators are `sine`, `saw`, `square`, `triangle`, and `noise`; format is `mono` or `stereo`.

Creation never overwrites an existing asset. A clean existing SoundCue is a no-op only when its single Wave-player node references the requested SoundWave. A clean existing MetaSound is a no-op only when document readback proves the exact generator, requested frequency (except noise), continuous-source mode, output format, and output connections. Otherwise the tool returns an `audio_asset_conflict` and leaves the asset untouched.

Mutations are blocked while PIE or SIE is active. MetaSound builder names and author metadata are neutral, and saved readback checks the document, generator node, and audio outputs for MCP-only references. If creation has already happened when a later build, save, or readback step fails, the structured failure sets `partial_mutation` and provides recovery guidance instead of encouraging a blind retry.

The companion is an authoring provider only. Finished SoundCue and MetaSound
assets must contain standard engine classes and must not persist
`/Script/UnrealMCP`, `/UnrealMCP`, `UnrealMCPMetaSound`, or another MCP-only
reference. Creation performs both in-memory and persisted dependency audits.
After authoring, the UnrealMCP plugins may be disabled or removed while the UE
plugins required by the authored asset remain enabled.

## Deliberate limits

- No session-scoped generic MetaSound graph editor in this pass.
- No audio playback, ambient actor spawning, source import, or level mutation.
- No UE 5.7/5.8 API or compatibility branch.
